<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabella I of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1451–<a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trastamara">House of Trastámara</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabella I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> was Queen of Castile who, with her husband Ferdinand of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a>, united the Spanish crowns. In 1492 they completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a> with the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> and sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s first voyage. Their reign laid the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabella-i-of-castile.jpg" alt="Isabella I of Castile" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IsabellaofCastile03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The marriage of John’s son Ferdinand II to <b>Isabella of Castile</b> in 1469 led to a dynastic union with the Crown of Castile from 1479, and from 1516 both crowns passed to the Habsburgs.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The marriage of <b>Isabella I of Castile</b> and Ferdinand II of Aragon in 1469 had joined their crowns in the person of the monarch, while each kingdom kept its own laws and institutions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The marriage of Ferdinand II of Aragon and <b>Isabella I of Castile</b> in 1469 then joined the Crowns of Aragon and Castile under the Catholic Monarchs, the foundation of the Spanish monarchy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…the first global empire in history, built with extraordinary speed after the dynastic union of the crowns of Castile and Aragon under <b>Isabella I of Castile</b> and Ferdinand II of Aragon, complete from 1479, and the conclusion of the Reconquista with the fall of Granada in January 1492.</blockquote><a href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The port city of Almería, part of the Nasrid emirate of Granada, submitted to the sovereignty of the Catholic Monarchs, Ferdinand II of Aragon and <b>Isabella I of Castile</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-22">22 December in history</a></li></ul></section>
